{"id":"f79a9b93c8b305e2a6045d100b8f9dea4d3e9817","axis":"silent","repo":"marko-js/marko","sha":"f79a9b93c8b305e2a6045d100b8f9dea4d3e9817","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/clean-yaks-see.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+\"@marko/runtime-tags\": patch","+---","+","+Report a repeated `value=` attribute on a core tag (`<let>`, `<return>`, `<script>`, `<const>`, `<if>`, …), or a repeated `valueChange=` on `<let>` or `<return>`, with one error that names the tag and links its docs, in place of `Invalid duplicate value attribute.` or an error calling the attribute unsupported."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"agent-feedback/items/2026-11-05-drop-the-default-check-from-let-value-lookup.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@","+---","+type: cleanup","+impact: low","+effort: low","+site: packages/runtime-tags/src/translator/core/let.ts › translate.exit","+---","+","+# Drop the `attr.default` test from `<let>`'s value lookup","+","+`<let>`'s translate finds its value with `attr.default || attr.name === \"value\"`, but the parser names every default attribute `value` (`packages/compiler/src/babel-plugin/parser.js` › `onAttrName` builds it as `t.markoAttribute(name || \"value\", …, !name)`), so `attr.default` never decides the match. Test the name alone.","+","+Check: `grep -n 'name || \"value\"' packages/compiler/src/babel-plugin/parser.js`; compile `<let/x=1/>` with the `attr.default ||` removed and see identical output."],"additions":12,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"agent-feedback/items/2026-11-05-validate-script-attributes-with-assertonlyvalueattr.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@","+---","+type: cleanup","+impact: low","+effort: low","+site: packages/runtime-tags/src/translator/core/script.ts › analyze","+---","+","+# Validate `<script>` attributes with `assertOnlyValueAttr`","+","+`<script>`'s analyze walks its attributes itself, tracking `seenValueAttr` to reject a second `value=` (through `buildDuplicateAttrError`) and any other attribute with its own \"does not support html attributes\" message, while every other single-value core tag gets both checks from `assertOnlyValueAttr` in `util/assert.ts`. Calling `assertOnlyValueAttr(tag, false, false, hint)` with the `html-script` suggestion as the hint would drop the loop and `seenValueAttr`, register the effect from the returned `valueAttr`, and span every unsupported attribute as the other tags do. It changes the wording the `error-script-attrs` fixture pins to \"only supports the `value=` attribute\", which is why it was left out of the duplicate-check consolidation.","+","+Check: compare the attribute loop in `core/script.ts` › `analyze` with `util/assert.ts` › `assertOnlyValueAttr`; compile `<script src=\"a.js\"/>` and read the message."],"additions":12,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/runtime-tags/src/__tests__/fixtures/error-let-duplicate-value-change/__snapshots__/error-compile-dom.debug.txt","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@","+","+    at packages/runtime-tags/src/__tests__/fixtures/error-let-duplicate-value-change/template.marko:1:36","+    > 1 | <let/x=input.a valueChange=input.b valueChange=input.c/>","+        |                                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ The [`<let>` tag](https://markojs.com/docs/reference/core-tag#let) takes a single `valueChange=` attribute.","+      2 | <div>${x}</div>","+      3 |","\\ No newline at end of file"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/runtime-tags/src/__tests__/fixtures/error-let-duplicate-value-change/__snapshots__/error-compile-dom.txt","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@","+","+    at packages/runtime-tags/src/__tests__/fixtures/error-let-duplicate-value-change/template.marko:1:36","+    > 1 | <let/x=input.a valueChange=input.b valueChange=input.c/>","+        |                                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ The [`<let>` tag](https://markojs.com/docs/reference/core-tag#let) takes a single `valueChange=` attribute.","+      2 | <div>${x}</div>","+   